1
00:05:12,631 --> 00:05:18,631
Monte Walsh is what the West was all about.

2
00:10:25,263 --> 00:10:31,263
Monte Walsh is a western film directed by William A. Fraker.

3
00:15:37,894 --> 00:15:43,894
Monte Walsh is an aging cowboy facing the ending days of the Wild West era.

4
00:20:50,526 --> 00:20:56,526
As barbed wire and railways steadily eliminate the need for the cowboy,
Monte and his friends are left with fewer and fewer options.

5
00:26:03,157 --> 00:26:09,157
New work opportunities are available to them, but the
freedom of the open prarie is what they long for.

6
00:31:15,789 --> 00:31:21,789
Eventually, they all must say goodbye to the lives
they knew, and try to make a new start.

7
00:36:28,421 --> 00:36:34,421
Monte Walsh, played by Lee Marvin.

8
00:41:41,052 --> 00:41:47,052
Martine Bernard, played by Jeanne Moreau.

9
00:46:53,684 --> 00:46:59,684
Chet Rollins, played by Jack Palance.

10
00:52:06,315 --> 00:52:12,315
Shorty Austin, played by Mitchell Ryan.

11
00:57:18,947 --> 00:57:24,947
Cal Brennan, played by Jim Davis.

12
01:02:31,578 --> 01:02:37,578
Hal Henderson, played by G. D. Spradlin.

13
01:07:44,210 --> 01:07:50,210
Monte Walsh is a 1970 American Western film
directed by cinematographer William A.

14
01:12:56,842 --> 01:13:02,842
Fraker (his directorial debut) starring Lee
Marvin, Jeanne Moreau and Jack Palance.

15
01:18:09,473 --> 01:18:15,473
The name "Monte Walsh" is taken from the title of a 1963 western novel by Jack
Schaefer, but the film has little to do with the plot of Schaefer's book.

16
01:23:22,105 --> 01:23:28,105
The film was set in Harmony, Arizona.

17
01:28:34,736 --> 01:28:40,736
The story has elements of a tragedy.

18
01:33:47,368 --> 01:33:53,368
The song played over the opening credits is "The Good Times Are Comin' " by
Mama Cass, with music and lyrics by John Barry and Hal David.
